    "q-143630": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143630",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A certain disease is present in $500$ out of $100\\,000$ people in city $A,$ $800$ out of $200\\,000$ people in city $B,$ and $1\\,100$ out of $500\\,000$ people in city $C.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected person from any city has the disease?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $D$ be the event that a person has the disease, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the person is from city $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the person is from city $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the person is from city $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person has the disease, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C)\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that there are a total of \n\n$$\n100\\,000+200\\,000+500\\,000=800\\,000\n$$\n\npeople in all three cities.\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap A),$ we take the number of people in city $A$ who have the disease $(500)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap A)=\\frac{500}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap B),$ we take the number of people in city $B$ who have the disease $(800)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap B)=\\frac{800}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\n- To calculate $P(D\\cap C),$ we take the number of people in city $C$ who have the disease $(1\\,100)$ and divide by the total number of people in the three cities $(800\\,000).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap C)=\\frac{1\\,100}{800\\,000}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person from any city has the disease is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =\\frac{500}{800\\,000}+\\frac{800}{800\\,000}+\\frac{1\\,100}{800\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\,400}{800\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{8\\,000} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1\\,000}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
