    "q-143529": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143529",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the components manufactured, $45%$ are produced by the first machine, $25%$ are produced by the second machine, and the third machine produces the remaining.\nIf $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, what is the probability that a randomly selected component is defective?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly selected component is defective, and \n\n- let ${B}_{1}$ be the event that the component was produced by the first machine,\n\n- let ${B}_{2}$ be the event that the component was produced by the second machine,\n\n- let ${B}_{3}$ be the event that the component was produced by the third machine.\n\nThen the disjoint union ${B}_{1}⊔{B}_{2}⊔{B}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected component is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap {B}_{1})+P(D\\cap {B}_{2})+P(D\\cap {B}_{3}) \\\\  & =P(D|{B}_{1})P({B}_{1})+P(D|{B}_{2})P({B}_{2})+P(D|{B}_{3})P({B}_{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the first machine produces $45%$ of the components, the second machine produces $25%$ of the components, the third machine produces the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(45%+25%)=30%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP({B}_{1})=0.45,\\,P({B}_{2})=0.25,\\,P({B}_{3})=0.3.\n$$\n\n- Since $8%$ of the components produced by the first machine, $4%$ produced by the second machine, and $5%$ produced by the third machine are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|{B}_{1})=0.08,\\,P(D|{B}_{2})=0.04,\\,P(D|{B}_{3})=0.05.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected component is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|{B}_{1})P({B}_{1})+P(D|{B}_{2})P({B}_{2})+P(D|{B}_{3})P({B}_{3}) \\\\  & =(0.08)(0.45)+(0.04)(0.25)+(0.05)(0.3) \\\\  & =0.036+0.01+0.015 \\\\  & =0.061.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
