    "q-143945": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143945",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "In a particular national park, there are three forests. Forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the park's total area, and $30%$ of the plants it contains are poisonous, while forest $B$ occupies $25%$ of the park's total area, and $20%$ of the plants it has are poisonous. Forest $C$ occupies the remaining area of the park. If the probability that a randomly selected plant from the park is poisonous is $0.24,$ what percentage of plants from forest $C$ are poisonous? Assume that the plants are evenly distributed throughout the park.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $V$ be the event that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the plant is from forest $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the plant is from forest $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the plant is from forest $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected plant is poisonous, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V\\cap A)+P(V\\cap B)+P(V\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.  \n\n- Since forest $A$ occupies $40%$ of the total park land and  forest $B$ occupies $25%$, then forest $C$ occupies the remaining\n\n$$\n100%-(40%+25%)=35%.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.4,\\,P(B)=0.25,\\,P(C)=0.35.\n$$\n\n- Since $30%$ of the plants in forest $A$ and $20%$ of the plants in forest $B$ are poisonous, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|A)=0.3,\\,P(V|B)=0.2\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected plant from the park is poisonous is $0.24,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(V)=0.24.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(V|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|A)P(A)+P(V|B)P(B)+P(V|C)P(C) \\\\ 0.24 & =(0.3)(0.4)+(0.2)(0.25)+P(V|C)(0.35) \\\\ 0.24 & =0.12+0.05+0.35P(V|C) \\\\ 0.35P(V|C) & =0.07 \\\\ P(V|C) & =0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20%$ of plants from forest $C$ are poisonous.",
